ifa/issues/160 -- an empty dict([]) next to a populated dict: once ifa/172 separates their CreationSets, the empty one's loops (__pyc_dict_from_iterable__'s `for pair in pairs` over [], dict.__str__'s `while i < self._len` with _len 0) are type-checked as live over a bottom element ('pair' has no type). Also fails at 752544ed, where the dicts were merged but the element union was still bottom-polluted. Flips to PASS when a loop over an empty container is treated as the dead code it is.
